      "text": "I've read the whole codebase. Let me analyze each ticket:\n\n1. **#212** — `paths.qualify()` says unqualified names belong to `schema` (default `etl_work`), but the code hardcodes `\"public\"`. Clear bug.\n2. **#215** — `retry.call_with_retry()` just calls `fn()` once; no retry loop at all. Also `is_transient` only knows `ConnectionError`/`TimeoutError`, so a partner-API HTTP error wouldn't be recognized as transient.\n3. **#219** — `guardrails.py` is a stub; needs a real policy (schema ownership boundaries, destructive-op approval, out-of-scope task refusal, URL scheme checks).\n4. **#223** — Router lowercases text but the `transformation`/`data_quality` patterns contain capitals (`\\bJoin\\b`, `\\bVerify\\b`...), so they can never match.\n5. **#224** — `format.message()` does `.encode(\"ascii\")`, which raises `UnicodeEncodeError` on non-ASCII names.\n\nLet me fix the straightforward ones first:",
